%erg 0.1
Title: erg-pr-merge aborts on a repo whose branches register no CI checks
Created: 2026-09-06
Author: sim

--- log ---
2026-09-06T17:20Z sim created

--- body ---
## Context
Observed on search-works-for-zotero PR #398, 2026-09-06. The script closed
and archived ticket 0720, pushed the close commit, then:

```
Queueing merge for PR #398...
GraphQL: Pull request Protected branch rules not configured for this branch (enablePullRequestAutoMerge)
Auto-merge unavailable — falling back to watch-then-merge...
no checks reported on the 't0720-arena-retention' branch
No checks registered yet (attempt 1/3) — waiting for CI to register...
(twice more)
erg-pr-merge: CI checks never registered after 3 attempts (no checks reported) — aborting merge
```

Exit 1, PR open, ticket already closed on the branch. The script is not
idempotent past the close step, so the documented recovery applied: a
direct `gh pr merge --merge`, which landed at once. Two other PRs in the
same repo the same evening (#390, #401, neither carrying a close commit)
took the auto-merge path and landed without a fallback.

Every PR in that repo reports an empty `statusCheckRollup`: no check ever
registers on its branches. The watch-then-merge fallback assumes a CI
that will eventually register, so on such a repo it can only die. The
"no checks reported" retry (ticket 0200) was written for the post-push
registration race, a different situation with the same message.

Why `--auto` failed on #398 and not on the other two is not isolated. The
one visible difference is the close-commit push just before the queue
attempt, which the script's own comment (around line 332) already
describes as leaving the forge's auto-merge failing briefly; the single
retry did not outlast it. Report the observation; do not build on the
guess.

## Relevant files
- `skills/merge/erg-pr-merge` — `watch_checks_or_die()` (about line 360) and the fallback branch after "Auto-merge unavailable" (about line 435)
- `tests/test_erg_pr_merge.sh` — where the mocked-forge case belongs
- `skills/merge/SKILL.md` — the bounce table; add the row for this bounce until the fix lands

## Actions
1. In the fallback, distinguish "checks not registered yet" from "this
   repo registers no checks": after the bounded retries, or before them,
   ask the forge whether the base branch has required checks and whether
   the PR's rollup is empty. When there is nothing to wait for and the PR
   is MERGEABLE, merge directly instead of dying. Keep dying when a check
   exists and is red or timed out.
2. Make the outcome legible: print which of the two cases was taken.
3. Add the bounce row to the merge skill's table meanwhile: "CI checks
   never registered" on a repo with no checks means finish with
   `gh pr merge --merge`; the close commit is already pushed.

## Test
- Mocked `gh` in `tests/test_erg_pr_merge.sh`: `pr checks --watch` answers
  "no checks reported" every time, `pr view` reports MERGEABLE with an
  empty rollup and no required checks. Red on the unfixed script (dies
  after the retries), green after (merges). A second case with one red
  check must still die.

## Verification
- [ ] Positive control recorded: the new test fails on the unfixed script
- [ ] A rerun against a no-checks repo lands the PR without manual `gh pr merge`
- [ ] The red-check case still aborts with the existing message

## Invariants
- Close-then-merge stays atomic from the caller's view; no new manual step
- The post-push registration race (ticket 0200) keeps its retries
- `make check` passes

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Fallback merges when the repo registers no checks and the PR is mergeable
- [ ] Test with a positive control in `tests/test_erg_pr_merge.sh`
- [ ] Bounce row in `skills/merge/SKILL.md`
